{
  "_comment": [
    "CONTROL-slot button grid. Modelled directly on the WigiDash LLMLauncherWidget's",
    "buttons.json (wigi-llm/wigidash/src/LLMLauncherWidget), which reads its config at",
    "runtime instead of hardcoding a table. Same idea here: ARRAY ORDER IS GRID ORDER,",
    "and adding / removing / reordering a button is a JSON edit — no rebuild, no redeploy",
    "of the device app. Restart the kiosk to pick up changes:",
    "  adb -s <serial> shell 'supervisorctl restart chromium'",
    "",
    "SECURITY: this file is the allowlist. The device NEVER sends a command — it sends a",
    "button id, and the service maps it here. argv is an argv ARRAY, executed with",
    "execFile and shell:false, so nothing is ever shell-interpreted. Keep it that way:",
    "a string command here would reintroduce the injection surface the array form removes.",
    "This file lives host-side and is not writable from the device.",
    "",
    "kind:",
    "  model  - a router preset. expectedModel is matched against the router's loaded/",
    "           loading ids to drive the active + loading treatments.",
    "  action - fires argv once. appendLoadedModel appends the currently-loaded model id",
    "           (router-control.sh unload REQUIRES a preset argument; a bare unload exits 1).",
    "  toggle - argv when `off`, stopArgv when `on`. on-ness comes from routerAvailable.",
    "",
    "requiresRouter: true  -> tile goes inert while the router is unreachable (the service",
    "                         400s these anyway; this makes it visible instead of silent).",
    "requiresLoadedModel: true -> tile goes inert while nothing is loaded (kill: the service",
    "                              400s 'no model loaded' anyway; same idea as requiresRouter,",
    "                              added 2026-08-11 after KILL rendered live with nothing to kill).",
    "",
    "argv/stopArgv entries below use the literal token ${CONTROL_SCRIPTS_DIR}, substituted at load",
    "time from the CONTROL_SCRIPTS_DIR env var (services/deviceinfo/server.js, loadButtons()) --",
    "point it at wherever YOUR fleet-control scripts (router-control.sh, start-router.sh) live.",
    "Left unset, these buttons fail per-action with ENOENT rather than crashing the service."
  ],
